HWO_TOOL_DESCRIPTION = "Compile or run an existing .hwo multi-agent workflow. Use action=compile for validation without execution. Before authoring or modifying HWO/HWG syntax, load the hwo-workflows skill; the native schema here intentionally stays compact."
HWO_COMM_TOOLS = "Communication tools:\n  - agent_send(to, message)        -> send a runtime mailbox message to your parent or your own child\n  - agent_receive(from, timeout?)  -> wait for a message from a specific member, default 60s\n  - agent_return({ \"name\": value }) -> submit declared outputs; this does not stop the agent\n\nMailbox messages are process coordination only. To export data to later agents\nor HWG, declare it in out(...) and include the same key in agent_return."
HWO_SYNTAX = "HWO workflow syntax:\n  @line [in(topic: string), out(report: file)]      optional file contract\n  #name# { ... }                                    named agent\n  #name# [in(x = $input.x), out(y: string)] { ... } agent I/O contract\n  #name@model# { ... }                              pin backend model from the available model table\n  (prompt.md)#name# { ... }                         bind custom system prompt\n  #name#(prompt.md) { ... }                         same, trailing form\n  // ... //                                         parallel block; agents only\n  ->                                                ordered todo item in the current agent run\n  ``` ... ```                                       comment block\n\nVariables and scope:\n  $input.x        workflow input, used in agent in(...) bindings or body text\n  $self.x         this agent's declared input/output value, used in body text\n  #agent.output   declared output from an already completed agent in the same sequence scope\n\nRules:\n  1. Use ``` ... ``` for comments. Do not use // for comments; // opens/closes a parallel block.\n  2. agent_return({ \"name\": value }) is the formal result. Only keys declared in out(...) are exported.\n  3. Consecutive -> items run as one ordered todo list in the same agent context. Do not call agent_return after each item.\n  4. Use -> for every step in a non-trivial agent body. Make agent_return the final -> step when out(...) is declared.\n  5. A parallel block may contain agents only. Parallel agents cannot read each other's #agent.output while running.\n  6. Use agent_send/agent_receive only for runtime coordination with your PARENT; mailbox messages are not structured outputs and parallel members cannot message each other.\n  7. After a parallel block finishes, later parent-scope agents may read declared outputs from its members.\n  8. Agent names are unique among siblings, including parallel members.\n  9. Prompt files use relative paths only; use ../ for parent directories.\n  10. Model pins use the exact model id after @, for example #research@deepseek-v4-flash#. Choose from the available model table when it is present.\n  11. Bind workflow inputs explicitly: #agent# [in(prompt = $input.prompt)] { -> Read $self.prompt ... }.\n  12. Never write in(prompt) in body text. in(...) is declaration/binding syntax only; use $input.prompt or $self.prompt in prose.\n  13. #agent.output is valid only in later in(...) bindings after that agent has completed. Do not use it inside a parallel sibling that runs at the same time.\n  14. If an agent writes a file that downstream agents need, declare out(fileName: file) and agent_return({ \"fileName\": \"path\" }).\n\nExample:\n  @line [in(prompt: string), out(deliverable: file)]\n\n  #architect# [in(prompt = $input.prompt), out(contract: file)] {\n    -> Read $self.prompt and identify the deliverable requirements.\n    -> Write the integration contract to build/contract.md.\n    -> Include exact file ownership, function signatures, globals, and dependency direction.\n    -> agent_return({ \"contract\": \"build/contract.md\" })\n  }\n\n  //\n    #scene_builder# [in(contract = #architect.contract), out(sceneFile: file)] {\n      -> Read $self.contract and implement only the scene module.\n      -> Write build/scene.js.\n      -> Do not modify player.js, environment.js, ui.js, or index.html.\n      -> agent_return({ \"sceneFile\": \"build/scene.js\" })\n    }\n    #player_builder# [in(contract = #architect.contract), out(playerFile: file)] {\n      -> Read $self.contract and implement only the player module.\n      -> Write build/player.js.\n      -> Do not modify scene.js, environment.js, ui.js, or index.html.\n      -> agent_return({ \"playerFile\": \"build/player.js\" })\n    }\n  //\n\n  #integrator# [\n    in(contract = #architect.contract, sceneFile = #scene_builder.sceneFile, playerFile = #player_builder.playerFile),\n    out(deliverable: file)\n  ] {\n    -> Read $self.contract, $self.sceneFile, and $self.playerFile.\n    -> Assemble the final artifact at build/index.html.\n    -> Verify the globals and initialization order required by the contract.\n    -> agent_return({ \"deliverable\": \"build/index.html\" })\n  }"
